WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.317 --> 00:00:01.150
(box clattering)

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:02.490
- [Narrator] Your last pizza probably came

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.260
in a box like this.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:07.290
It's cardboard, sturdy
and most importantly,

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.660
keeps your cheese from
getting stuck to the lid.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.670
And that's thanks to Domino's.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.410
This founder is widely credited

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.660
with creating the corrugated pizza box.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.060
It's just one of the
company's innovations,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.420
not in pizza, but in delivery.
(doorbell ringing)

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.410
In 2022, more than 40%
of online delivery orders

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:28.410
for major pizza chains were from Domino's.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.240
Here's how the company made its name

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.920
in the pizza delivery market

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.570
and why this foundational piece

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.750
of its business is facing new challenges.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.333
This is the economics of Domino's.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:43.740
♪ Domino's Pizza delivers ♪

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.470
- [Narrator] Domino's,
originally called DomiNick's,

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.090
acquired its first restaurant

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.880
in 1960 in Ypsilanti, Michigan,

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.790
and jumped into the delivery
business the same year.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:57.210
Something very few restaurants
were doing at the time.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:59.370
- Now we think of delivery
as being so ubiquitous.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.560
I mean, so many types of
restaurants have delivery

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.700
but Domino's was there
very early at scale.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.800
- [Narrator] One reason
it's become so well known

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.200
for its delivery is a
campaign the company started

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.870
in the '80s promising delivery in.

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:14.280
- [Announcer 1] Less than 30 minutes.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.360
- [Announcer 2] Within 30 minutes.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.890
- [Announcer 3] Only
Domino's Pizza delivers

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.180
in 30 minutes or less.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.830
- People really did have the sense

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.570
that once they ordered that pizza,

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.370
they were gonna get it
to their homes quickly

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:25.920
and I think that really
helped for marketing.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.740
- [Narrator] Domino's ended
that guarantee in 1993

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.980
after a delivery driver struck
another vehicle resulting

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.330
in a lawsuit.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:36.930
But by then, the company had
cemented its place in delivery

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.130
and in the half century

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.533
since Domino's was founded, it's paid off.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:45.033
It took the biggest slice of
pizza chain sales in 2022.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:48.210
Domino's success is due in part

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:51.480
to creativity in every step
of its delivery process,

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.670
starting with stores.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:57.660
Many are small and often with
little or no dining space,

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.430
a model the company has said allowed

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:02.640
for lower rents and
reduced store expenses.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.540
Over the years.,

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.850
Domino's has also focused
on establishing more

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.700
than 6,500 locations in the US

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.060
and has worked with franchisees
to extend their reach.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.220
- So one part of Domino's strategy

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.930
is what's called fortressing,

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.630
which is making sure
there's enough pizza shops

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:23.490
in a certain mile radius,
that wherever your order goes,

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.260
one of those pizza shops can handle it

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:28.140
and it can help get it
to your house quickly.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.240
- [Narrator] The company
supply line is also structured

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.950
to make the pizza creation process

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.290
as quick and uniform as possible.

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:36.510
Domino's has 25 supply chain centers

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.550
in the US where dough is mixed

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.130
and toppings are prepared
before being sold

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:45.150
to franchise stores where
pizzas are assembled and baked.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.590
The more pizzas that are sold,

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:49.560
the more money Domino's
makes from its supply chain.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:53.880
It made up 59% of
Domino's revenue in 2021.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.250
The next part of the process is ordering.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:58.500
In 2008, the company rolled out

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:00.840
its advanced online ordering system,

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.000
which included a customized pizza builder

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.710
and the Pizza Tracker.

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.920
- So the Pizza Tracker is
something that Domino's invented.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.010
They will let you know
where it is in the process.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.330
It's whether it's being cooked,

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:15.750
whether it's out for delivery,
where they're approaching.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.980
- [Narrator] Domino's has continued

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:19.170
to introduce new ordering options.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:22.590
- Pizza emoji scent, Domino's
ordered, smiley face.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.020
- [Narrator] Then there's
the last step of the process,

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:28.080
getting the pizza from
the kitchen to your home.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.370
From working with special kinds

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:32.850
of insulated bags to
creating 3D car top signs,

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.790
Domino's has been a big
innovator in this step.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:38.400
The company has experimented
with several methods

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.779
of delivery vehicles,

00:03:39.779 --> 00:03:42.240
(helicopter whirring)
helicopters, electric bikes,

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:46.050
self-driving cars, even cars
with a heated pizza oven.

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:48.540
- It's really putting the whole brand

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.250
behind delivery in a lot of ways.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.560
- [Narrator] But after years
at the top of delivery,

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.110
Domino's is facing new challenges.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.347
Companies like Uber Eats, GrubHub

00:03:57.347 --> 00:04:00.990
and DoorDash are eating at
Domino's business in the US

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:04.800
as drivers leave pizza for
apps with more flexible hours.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:05.640
It's contributed

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.730
to an industry-wide
delivery driver shortage.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:10.320
Other chains like Papa John's

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:12.480
and Pizza Hut have both started working

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.600
with some of these apps,
but Domino's has resisted.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.270
- They argue that that
makes it more profitable

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:21.720
because you're not having
to pay an outside service

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:25.470
to deliver that pizza and to
market that pizza on their app

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:28.020
and it keeps 'em closer
to their customers.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:30.030
- [Narrator] As the company
has faced these issues,

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:33.900
its shares have slumped from
a high at the end of 2021.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.960
Now Domino's is exploring new options.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.550
The company is building out a fleet

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:41.610
of electric delivery vehicles
to recruit new drivers

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:44.760
and it's now offering customers
what it calls a $3 tip

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.560
to pick up their own pie.

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:49.080
- [Announcer 4] We see
you, carry out heroes.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:50.926
- You know, it's much cheaper for them

00:04:50.926 --> 00:04:53.550
if their customers pick up their own pizza

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:56.970
and so they are getting in
the pickup game in a big way.

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:58.620
- [Narrator] As Domino's
continues to grapple

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.216
with these issues, investors

00:05:00.216 --> 00:05:04.298
and customers will be watching
for future innovations.

00:05:04.298 --> 00:05:06.965
(lively music)

